# binance-klines — daily closes finalizer (cron)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `main.py update` downloads Binance's official daily 1m archives (trailing
# 14-day window) and finalizes them into daily_closes.parquet. The running stream
# does NOT do this — it only keeps the live buffer and writes a *provisional*
# close near midnight. Without this cron, daily_closes.parquet freezes at that
# provisional snapshot and downstream consumers silently degrade (NaN signals).
#
# The 14-day re-check window makes every run idempotent and self-healing against
# Binance's staggered 1-2 day archive publication.
#
# INSTALL into ROOT's crontab — the container runs as root, so both `docker` and
# the root-owned logs/ dir require it:
#
#     ( sudo crontab -l 2>/dev/null; cat deploy/binance-update.cron ) | sudo crontab -
#     sudo crontab -l          # verify
#
# TIMEZONE: uncomment the CRON_TZ line below to pin the schedule to UTC (Vixie/cronie
# support it; some minimal crons — e.g. busybox — do not, and will error with
# "bad minute"). If you leave it commented, times run in the system timezone —
# confirm it is UTC with `date +%Z`, otherwise shift the 23:30 line so it still
# lands just before your strategy's pre-midnight (UTC) cache read.
#
# PATH: adjust /home/ev/projects/binance-klines to your checkout, and `binance-data`
# to your container name if you changed it. NOTE: in ROOT's crontab, `~` expands to
# /root, not your home — always use the absolute path shown below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#CRON_TZ=UTC

# Finalize the day just before the strategy's ~23:45 UTC cache read.
30 23 * * *     cd /home/ev/projects/binance-klines && docker exec binance-data python main.py update >> logs/update.log 2>&1

# Catch each symbol's official archive as Binance publishes them through the day.
0 5,11,17 * * * cd /home/ev/projects/binance-klines && docker exec binance-data python main.py update >> logs/update.log 2>&1
